  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#nonce-attributes says:\r\n\r\n> Elements that have a [nonce](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#attr-nonce) content attribute ensure that the cryptographic nonce is only exposed to script (and not to side-channels like CSS attribute selectors) by taking the value from the content attribute, moving it into an internal slot named [[CryptographicNonce]], exposing it to script via the [HTMLOrSVGElement](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#htmlorsvgelement) interface mixin, and setting the content attribute to the empty string. Unless otherwise specified, the slot's value is the empty string.\r\n\r\nWhen exactly does that happen?\r\n\r\nIn Gecko, we do it when the element becomes connected. In Blink and WebKit it seems to happen when the element is bound to any tree, even disconnected, which feels a bit weird.",
